# Mobile — navigate with known interactive state

A push must not paint a guess and then correct it. If the source already knows subscribe,
notification, or download state — or the device already has it in a synchronous memory cache —
the destination's first frame uses that value.

This is the same first-paint habit as **mobile-image-loading** (artwork) and
**mobile-section-chrome-cache** (section chips), applied to controls that flip meaning when they
are wrong: Subscribe vs Unsubscribe, the notification bell, download vs delete.

## Do

- Before `navigation.navigate`, pass every control state the source already painted or can read
  synchronously (`previewIsSubscribed`, cached notification flag, numeric `channelId` when known).
  Use the entity's `build*DetailParams` helper so callers cannot forget a field the header needs.
- Keep a **synchronous in-memory cache** of subscribe + notification lookup (hydrated with SQLite
  at `initializeDatabase`, updated on subscribe / unsubscribe / bell toggle). Deep links and
  Browse read it on first paint; do not wait for `isSubscribed()` or `GET /channel/:id`.
- Seed `useState` from preview params or that cache. An async SQLite confirm is allowed only when
  it will not change the first frame.
- Resolve the notification bell by `channelIdText` (cached numeric id + account rows), not by
  waiting for the channel DTO's numeric `id`.
- Hydrate `downloadStore` at bootstrap so list-row download/delete icons read the real status on
  the first frame of the destination, including during the push transition.
- When adding a new detail control that has on/off or download/delete meaning, add it to this
  cache and to the navigate params in the same change. Do not introduce a default and "fix it
  when the request returns."

## Don't

- Don't default Subscribe / bell-off / download-outline and then flip after a repository or
  network read. That flash is the bug.
- Don't `await` SQLite, `/auth/me`, or `GET /channel/:id` before `navigate` just to populate
  these params. Read memory (and pass what the row already showed). Prefetch stays fire-and-forget
  (**mobile-image-loading**).
- Don't look up account notification rows only by numeric `channel.id` that arrives with the
  detail DTO. The id text is known at tap time.
- Don't treat "Downloaded only" Home rows as subscribed. Pass `previewIsSubscribed: false` there.

